Xdelta 3 NEWS

Please file bug reports at https://github.com/jmacd/xdelta/issues.


** Changes in version 3.2.2

* Handle allocation failures throughout the encoder, decoder, merge, and
  application-header paths without leaking memory or dereferencing null
  pointers.

* Require the complete XZ magic signature before invoking external
  decompression.

** Changes in version 3.2.1

* Support standard input as the source file when encoding or decoding.

* Support Unicode file names on Windows.

* Reject invalid armor streams before decoding and harden application-header
  file-name handling.

* Correct secondary-compression status and header reporting, and accept the
  documented smaller source-window sizes.

* Restore the C++ regression suite, port it to Windows, and exercise source
  copies beyond 2 GiB.

* Install the reusable library and public headers, document CMake consumer
  workflows, and verify that public headers are independently portable.

* Add dependency-free Windows x86 release binaries alongside the existing
  x86-64 and ARM64 packages.

* Show command help when invoked without arguments from an interactive
  terminal.
